exports[`English legal content: [Function Disclaimer] 1`] = `
{
  "labels": [],
  "meta": [
    [
      "description",
      "Plain-language risk summary for MyQRLWallet, the self-custody wallet for QRL 2.0 by DigitalGuards.",
    ],
    [
      "keywords",
      "QRL, QRL 2.0, Quantum Resistant Ledger, post-quantum blockchain, QRL wallet, web wallet, cryptocurrency wallet",
    ],
  ],
  "text": "DisclaimerLast updated: 13 July 2026This is a short, plain-language summary of the most important points about MyQRLWallet. It is provided for convenience only. Our Terms of Use govern your use of the software, and in case of any conflict the Terms of Use control.What MyQRLWallet isMyQRLWallet is free, open-source, self-custody client software for the QRL 2.0 blockchain. It lets you generate keys on your own device, view your balances, sign transactions locally and broadcast them to the QRL network. It is provided by DigitalGuards.You are in sole control of your fundsDigitalGuards does not hold, control or have access to your crypto-assets, private keys or recovery phrase, and cannot move, freeze, recover, reverse or return your funds. Your keys and recovery phrase are generated and stored only on your device. If you lose them, no one, including DigitalGuards, can recover them or your funds.Risks to be aware ofBlockchain transactions are irreversible. A transaction sent to a wrong address cannot be undone.You are responsible for safeguarding your device, PIN or password, and recovery phrase.Phishing and malware are real threats. Always verify you are using the official MyQRLWallet.QRL 2.0 is currently a testnet. Testnet tokens have no value and the network may be reset without notice.The QRL network and any third-party contracts, tokens or dApps you interact with are outside our control and may fail or behave unexpectedly.No fees, no adviceDigitalGuards charges no fee for MyQRLWallet. Network fees are paid to the QRL network, not to us. Nothing in MyQRLWallet is financial, investment, legal or tax advice.LiabilityOur liability is set out in section 7 of the Terms of Use. That section preserves all liability that cannot be excluded under mandatory law, including for death or personal injury, intent or conscious recklessness, and product liability.Restricted jurisdictionsMyQRLWallet may not be used by anyone located in, resident in or acting for a sanctioned jurisdiction or by any sanctioned person. The full sanctions terms are in section 5 of the Terms of Use.Who we are and how to reach usMyQRLWallet is a product of DigitalGuards (eenmanszaak, Netherlands), KvK 91987482. Full details are in the Imprint. To report a security issue, see our Security Policy or email security@digitalguards.nl.",
  "title": "Disclaimer | MyQRLWallet",
}
`;

